    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "influxdb",
        "uid": "P3C6603E967DC8568"
      },
      "description": "The only real capacity-fade signal this system has. Each point is one charge session: charge_ah divided by the SoC it added, i.e. pack amp-hours per 100 points of raw BMS SoC. The BMS-reported SoH cannot be used for this -- it is pinned at exactly 100.0 and has never moved (see the SoC & SoH panel below).\n\nMeasured 2026-09-05 over 32 sessions with a SoC delta of 14 points or more: 84.3 Ah per 100 raw-SoC points, with AC (28 sessions, ~1 kW) and DC rapid (4 sessions, 44-56 kW) charging agreeing to within 0.8%. Scatter between sessions is about 2.3 Ah, so read the trend, never a single point.\n\nSessions below 14 SoC points are excluded: the same absolute coulomb-counting error over a smaller denominator makes them far noisier (a 1.5-point session came out at 86.7 Ah, a 2-point one at 95.0 Ah).\n\nRaw-SoC is not the dashboard percentage. Measured over 2861 paired samples, display = -1.687 + 1.0665 x raw, so the window the driver sees is 93.77 raw points wide. Multiply by that to convert this axis into usable capacity.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
