      },
      "description": "Rest-only cell spread, from the BMS max/min pair.\n\nREAD THE QUANTISATION FIRST: the BMS reports cell voltages in 0.02 V steps, so this series can only ever take the values 0, 20, 40, 60 mV and so on. Over the 7.5 weeks to 2026-09-05 the mean was 10.5 mV, i.e. it alternates between 0 and one step -- every one of the 96 cells sits in the same bin. The 50 mV warning threshold therefore means \"three steps or more\", and a drifting cell is invisible here until it has drifted a full 20 mV.\n\n\"Outlier cell #\" is meaningless while the spread is 0: with every cell in one bin the tie-break resolves to the lowest index, which is why it reads 1 or 2 so often. Trust it only when the spread is at least 40 mV.\n\nThe y-axis is capped at 150 mV. The only five readings above 50 mV in the whole history (260, 440 and 3800 mV) were all garbage frames between 2026-07-15 and 2026-07-24, before the plausibility guard added in #1421; there have been none since.",
